#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0172 expect=violation domain=SS
#note "W5 phase 0 (PLAN-grouped-aggregate-functions): the cross-dataset broadcast's 'no group' answer. max_date(DSSTDTC, domain=\"DS\", group=[USUBJID]) is grouped on DS and read per SS row by USUBJID. Subject A has DS rows and an earlier SSDTC -> fires (row 1). Subject B is DEAD in SS but has NO DS row at all: its key finds no group, the binding is missing for it, and `date(SSDTC) < missing` does not fire (row 2 quiet). DS also carries subject C, which has no SS row: a foreign group nobody reads is simply unused. This Check has no `USUBJID in $…` guard, so the quiet row 2 IS the broadcast default being read. GREEN on the pre-port engine (cumba-corej@8513690): pins what stands."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=A
dataset SS label="Subject Status"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SSSTRESC type=Char label="Character Result/Finding in Std Format"
col SSDTC type=Char label="Date/Time of Collection"
---
S1 | SS | A | DEAD | 2013-01-01
S1 | SS | B | DEAD | 2013-01-01
---

dataset DS label=Disposition
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ type=Num label="Sequence Number"
col DSSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | A | 1 | 2014-01-14
S1 | DS | A | 2 | 2014-07-02
S1 | DS | C | 1 | 2014-07-02
---
